Lumen OS: volume keys to a projector card while it asks for them (Play 6 zoom and shift, stock parity).

On a TV (mUseTvRouting) PhoneWindowManager.interceptKeyBeforeDispatching never lets VOLUME UP / DOWN / MUTE
reach the focused window. Stock XGIMI firmware has a key intercept service (IGimiCommon.registerInterceptKey)
that its zoom and shift window uses to take VOLUME UP / DOWN for the picture size. Lumen has no such service.
While sys.lumen.volkeys_until holds an uptime in the future (the projector app sets it when the card opens and
refreshes it on every key, at most about a minute ahead), the volume keys go to the focused window; otherwise
nothing changes. A crashed app gives the keys back when the time runs out. Device-neutral, Play 6 base only.

diff -ruN a/frameworks/base/services/core/java/com/android/server/policy/PhoneWindowManager.java b/frameworks/base/services/core/java/com/android/server/policy/PhoneWindowManager.java
--- a/frameworks/base/services/core/java/com/android/server/policy/PhoneWindowManager.java	2026-10-24 11:45:02
+++ b/frameworks/base/services/core/java/com/android/server/policy/PhoneWindowManager.java	2026-10-24 11:45:03
@@ -4165,6 +4165,12 @@
             case KeyEvent.KEYCODE_VOLUME_DOWN:
             case KeyEvent.KEYCODE_VOLUME_MUTE:
                 if (mUseTvRouting || mHandleVolumeKeysInWM) {
+                    // Lumen OS: while a projector adjustment card asks for them (the zoom and shift card
+                    // of the Play 6, where stock uses VOLUME UP / DOWN for the size), the volume keys go to
+                    // the focused window, as stock XGIMI's key intercept service did.
+                    if (lumenVolumeKeysToApp()) {
+                        break;
+                    }
                     // On TVs or when the configuration is enabled, volume keys never
                     // go to the foreground app.
                     dispatchDirectAudioEvent(event);
@@ -6049,6 +6055,15 @@
             Log.e(TAG, "Error dispatching volume key in handleVolumeKey for event:"
                     + event, e);
         }
+    }
+
+    /**
+     * Lumen OS: true while sys.lumen.volkeys_until holds an uptime (ms) in the future. The projector app sets it
+     * when its card opens and refreshes it on every key, so a crash gives the keys back within a minute.
+     */
+    private static boolean lumenVolumeKeysToApp() {
+        final long until = SystemProperties.getLong("sys.lumen.volkeys_until", 0L);
+        return until > 0L && SystemClock.uptimeMillis() < until;
     }
 
     @Nullable
